---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
---

<Base title="How it works" description="How Unfleece keeps your PDF files private: everything runs in your browser via WebAssembly. No file upload, no account, no fleeceware.">
  <section class="section" style="padding-top:2.5rem">
    <div class="container content-width">
      <div class="section-head" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem">
        <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
        <h1 class="h1">Your files never leave your browser.</h1>
        <p class="body-lg ink-soft" style="margin-top:.75rem; max-width:60ch">
          Unfleece runs every PDF operation locally via WebAssembly. There is no server that
          receives, stores, or processes your documents — which is exactly why it can be free.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div id="privacy" class="reassure glass" style="scroll-margin-top:84px">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow accent-text" style="display:block;margin-bottom:.75rem">Don't trust us — verify it</span>
          <h2 class="h2">Prove it's private in 10 seconds.</h2>
          <p class="body">Don't take our word for it. Watch the network while you work — no document is uploaded. If a tool errors and reports are enabled, you may also see the content-blind <code>/api/err</code> request described below. The source is open, so you can read exactly what it does.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="steps">
          <div class="step"><span class="n">1</span><p><strong>Open any tool</strong> and press F12 → Network tab.</p></div>
          <div class="step"><span class="n">2</span><p><strong>Run it on a file.</strong> Watch the request list.</p></div>
          <div class="step"><span class="n">3</span><p><strong>See no file upload.</strong> Turn off Wi-Fi — it still works.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="tool-section" id="telemetry">
        <span class="eyebrow">The one exception, in the open</span>
        <h2 class="h2">Content-blind error reports</h2>
        <p class="body ink-soft" style="max-width:64ch">
          When a tool errors, Unfleece sends a single tiny report so we can find and fix bugs we can't
          see otherwise. It contains <strong>only</strong> which tool failed, an error category, the engine,
          your browser family and language — <strong>never</strong> your files, file names, error text, or any
          identifier. It honors your browser's Do&#8209;Not&#8209;Track, and you can turn it off here:
        </p>
        <label class="checkbox-row" style="margin-top:1rem">
          <input type="checkbox" id="telemetry-toggle" checked />
          <span class="checkbox-box"><Icon name="check" /></span>
          Send content-blind error reports
        </label>
        <p class="help" id="telemetry-state" style="margin-top:.5rem"></p>
        <script is:inline>
          (function () {
            var box = document.getElementById('telemetry-toggle');
            var state = document.getElementById('telemetry-state');
            if (!box || !state) return;
            var dnt = navigator.doNotTrack === '1' || navigator.doNotTrack === 'yes' || window.doNotTrack === '1';
            function read() { try { return localStorage.getItem('uf-telemetry') !== 'off'; } catch (e) { return null; } }
            function render() {
              if (dnt) { box.checked = false; box.disabled = true; state.textContent = 'Off — your browser sends Do-Not-Track, which we honor.'; return; }
              var enabled = read();
              if (enabled === null) { box.checked = false; box.disabled = true; state.textContent = 'Off — browser storage is unavailable, so reports are disabled.'; return; }
              box.checked = enabled;
              state.textContent = box.checked ? 'On — content-blind error reports help us fix bugs.' : 'Off — no reports are sent.';
            }
            render();
            box.addEventListener('change', function () {
              try { localStorage.setItem('uf-telemetry', box.checked ? 'on' : 'off'); } catch (e) {}
              render();
            });
          })();
        </script>
      </section>

      <section class="tool-section">
        <span class="eyebrow">Why it's free</span>
        <h2 class="h2">No server, no bill, no paywall</h2>
        <p class="body ink-soft" style="max-width:64ch">
          Because all the work happens on your computer, Unfleece has no compute or bandwidth bill —
          so there's nothing to monetize with a trial trap. The fleeceware sites charge you for
          something your own device can already do.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="tool-section">
        <span class="eyebrow">Honest about limits</span>
        <h2 class="h2">What it can and can't do</h2>
        <div class="compare">
          <div class="col us">
            <h3 class="h4">What works great</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><Icon name="check" /> Merge, split, rotate, organize, crop</li>
              <li><Icon name="check" /> Images ↔ PDF, PDF → images / text</li>
              <li><Icon name="check" /> Watermark, page numbers, metadata, sign</li>
              <li><Icon name="check" /> Lossless optimize & compress</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="col them">
            <h3 class="h4">Honest caveats</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><Icon name="alert" /> Very large files are bound by your device memory</li>
              <li><Icon name="alert" /> PDF→Text is selectable text only (scans need OCR)</li>
              <li><Icon name="alert" /> Compress uses Ghostscript; raster fallback is image-only</li>
              <li><Icon name="alert" /> We label every tool for what it actually does</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="tool-section">
        <span class="eyebrow">Open source</span>
        <h2 class="h2">Auditable by design</h2>
        <p class="body ink-soft" style="max-width:64ch">
          Unfleece is released under the AGPL-3.0 license. Contributions, audits, and self-hosting are
          welcome — <a class="btn-link" href="https://github.com/darekhta/Unfleece" target="_blank" rel="noopener">view the source on GitHub ↗</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
